From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Sutcliffe <dansut@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: fix Hinlink H68K GMAC1 PHY reset pin
 conflict

In rk3568-hinlink-opc.dtsi, &i2s1_8ch lacks an explicit pinctrl definition,
causing the audio driver to claim the default 8-channel i2s1m0 pin group.
This conflicts with gmac1_rstn (GPIO1_B0), holding the RTL8211F PHY in
reset and causing the probe to fail with -ENODEV.

Add explicit pinctrl-0 to &i2s1_8ch in rk3568-hinlink-h68k.dts to release
GPIO1_B0 and allow the GMAC1 PHY to initialize properly.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Sutcliffe <dansut@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-hinlink-h68k.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-hinlink-h68k.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-hinlink-h68k.dts
@@ -81,3 +81,14 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The audio codec (&i2s1_8ch) in rk3568-hinlink-opc.dtsi lacks an explicit
+ * pinctrl definition, causing the driver to claim the default 8-channel
+ * i2s1m0 pin group. This group includes GPIO1_B0, which conflicts with
+ * gmac1_rstn above, holding the RTL8211F PHY in reset and failing probe (-ENODEV).
+ */
+&i2s1_8ch {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&i2s1m0_sclkrx &i2s1m0_lrckrx &i2s1m0_sdi0 &i2s1m0_sdo0>;
+};
